## Summary

Before: documents had no explicit whole-document replacement relationship, and Ask treated newer documents as superseding older ones generally.
Now: DOCUMENT.superseded_by declares replacement. Uploads accept supersedes, staged writes flatten chains, and loads and writes reject cycles. This supports cumulative weekly gradeband decks without guessing replacement from titles, dates or URLs. The completed TODO for issue #178 is removed.

Before: search and document reading could present older versions without replacement guidance.
Now: search favors current matches and scans past superseded-only results. A shared resolver follows sheet-loaded chains to the latest replacement. Reading retains historical text and annotates affected descendants, including attachments inside an email. Notices require access to the latest replacement; consent hiding suppresses the link while retaining historical documents, extracts and reminders.

Before: uploading bytes X, then Y, then X failed cycle validation.
Now: following the lead's narrower direction, one transaction makes the original X document current again and points Y to it. Its original metadata remains; no separate revision records the reversion. Retries reuse the document and content. Other cycles are refused; referenced replacements cannot be deleted until incoming links are cleared or repointed.

Deliberately excluded: an automatic gradeband importer, inferred replacement, and automatic reminder completion or migration. Existing permissions govern reads and super-admin writes. Production createtabs succeeded, checking six spreadsheets and installing DOCUMENT.superseded_by.

Main's PDF-page functionality was preserved by combining schema, permission, fixture and TODO changes, without substantive redesign. The latest requested merge reported already up to date; no new conflicts or merge commit were needed. Database, tools, Ask and PDF-thumbnail suites and repository-wide vet passed in prior merge verification; the latest verification reruns are recorded in the turn.

